So, at face value, it looks like chaotic elvish
wizards get start-scummed a lot more than lawful
dwarvish valkyries.

The role stats mostly don't surprise me very much.
Everything with a chance at a magic marker, for
example, has rather poor numbers, and everything
that always starts with a longsword has pretty
good numbers.  Not astonishing.

Alignment, correlates more strongly than I
would have guessed, but I haven't controlled
for the fact that alignment correlates rather
strongly with role, which may be relevant.

Look at the race numbers, though.  Wow.
Such a sharp division between Elf/Orc/Gno
and Hum/Dwa cannot be entirely explained
by role correlation.  Elves have an even
worse stat than wizards (though I didn't
calculate whether the small difference is
statistically significant).  I wonder if
somebody is start scumming elves in
particular for certain starting attributes,
and if so which attributes.  Not having
played many elves myself yet, I'm not
clear on all the strategic points there.


